# What must never be committed, and why.
#
# Three kinds of thing live here: build output (regenerated, huge, conflicts on every pull),
# machine-specific config (correct for one computer and wrong for everyone else), and secrets
# (a signing key committed once is a signing key leaked forever).

### Build output ###
.gradle/
build/
captures/
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/
release/
*.apk
*.aab
# Heap dumps from the Android Studio profiler. Large, and can contain whatever was in memory.
*.hprof
*.log

### Machine-specific ###
# Holds the Android SDK path, which differs on every computer. Android Studio recreates it when the
# project is opened, so it is never worth committing — and committing it breaks everyone else's build.
local.properties

### Secrets ###
# Release signing material. Never commit any of it: anyone holding the key can publish an update
# that phones will accept as genuine.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
keystore.properties
signing.properties
secrets.properties

# The Gradle wrapper jar IS committed on purpose — it is what lets ./gradlew work on a machine with
# no Gradle installed, which is the whole point of the wrapper. This line protects it in case a
# global ignore rule excludes *.jar.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

### Android Studio / IntelliJ ###
# Most of .idea/ is shared project config worth committing — compiler, gradle, misc,
# runConfigurations. The entries below are per-developer or regenerated on every open, so they churn
# constantly and conflict for no reason.
*.iml
.idea/caches/
.idea/libraries/
.idea/modules.xml
.idea/workspace.xml
.idea/shelf/
.idea/navEditor.xml
.idea/assetWizardSettings.xml
.idea/deploymentTargetSelector.xml
.idea/deploymentTargetDropDown.xml
.idea/androidTestResultsUserPreferences.xml
.idea/appInsightsSettings.xml
.idea/studiobot.xml
out/
!**/src/main/**/out/
!**/src/test/**/out/

### Kotlin ###
# Kotlin 2.x build session data.
.kotlin

### Other editors ###
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

### Claude Code ###
# Shared project instructions can be committed; this file holds one developer's own permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json

### Operating systems ###
# A mixed room will produce all of these.
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.directory
